# EazeNote environment variables: NAMES ONLY.
#
# How to use this file
#   1. Copy it to a new file called ".env.local" (that file is git-ignored and never uploaded).
#   2. Put the real values in ".env.local" on your own computer.
#   3. On Vercel, add the same names under Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# Rules
#   - Never put a real key in this file, in the code, in a chat, or in an email.
#   - Never start a secret's name with NEXT_PUBLIC_. That prefix copies the value
#     into the JavaScript every visitor's browser downloads.
#   - Set a spending limit on every provider account before creating its key.
#
# Phase 1 (screens with sample data) needs none of these. They are listed so the
# names are agreed before Phase 2 and 3.

# --- Phase 2: login and database (Supabase) ---------------------------------
# The project URL and the "publishable" (anon) key are designed to be public,
# so they are the only values allowed to use the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# The service-role key bypasses every database rule. Server only.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Phase 3: speech-to-text and AI drafting --------------------------------
VULAVULA_API_KEY=
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Phase 4: email sending (Resend) ----------------------------------------
RESEND_API_KEY=
